WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
Tomorrow, Jo will face a choice.

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.390
Tell the truth, or tell a lie.

3
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.590
But suppose God knows today
exactly what Jo will do tomorrow.

4
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.580
Then Jo's act seems already fixed.

5
00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.280
The philosopher Boethius saw the danger.

6
00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:19.060
If acts are fixed, rewards
and punishments look unjust,

7
00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.060
and prayer looks pointless.

8
00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:24.230
So if God already knows
what you will choose,

9
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.560
is your choice still yours?

10
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:30.460
In this mission, you'll explore
two ways God could be eternal:

11
00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:34.800
outside time altogether, or
living through every moment.

12
00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:37.960
Then you'll compare three
answers, from Swinburne,

13
00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.320
Boethius and Anselm, and
weigh up what each one costs.

14
00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:47.650
Your mission: weigh up whether a choice
God already knows can still be yours.
